---
import { formatPrice, pricing } from "../data/pricing";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import Prose from "../layouts/prose.astro";

// TODO: draft terms. Have them reviewed by a lawyer before launch.
---

<Prose
	title="Terms of service"
	description={`The terms that apply when you use ${site.name} or enrol in a cohort.`}
	updated={new Date("2026-09-24")}
>
	<blockquote>
		<p>These terms are a draft and are being reviewed before cohort enrolment opens online.</p>
	</blockquote>

	<p>
		These terms apply to your use of the {site.name} website and to any cohort
		you enrol in. {site.name} is operated by {site.company}. By enrolling, you
		agree to these terms.
	</p>

	<h2>Enrolment</h2>
	<p>
		Your seat is held once we accept your application and receive your {formatPrice(pricing.deposit)} deposit. The rest of the fee is due before
		the cohort starts, or in instalments if you chose a payment plan.
	</p>

	<h2>Refunds</h2>
	<p>
		If you withdraw within {pricing.refundDays} days of your cohort starting, we
		refund everything you've paid except the deposit. After that, fees aren't
		refundable, but you can ask to transfer to a later cohort once.
	</p>

	<h2>Your work</h2>
	<p>
		You and your team own the code you write. Work on your own startup in weeks
		13 to 15 belongs to that startup. You give us permission to show your
		cloned product at demo day and, with your agreement, in our marketing.
	</p>

	<h2>Conduct</h2>
	<p>
		Cohorts only work when teammates can rely on each other. We may remove
		anyone who harasses others, shares other students' work without permission
		or repeatedly misses their team's commitments, after a warning.
	</p>

	<h2>Our materials</h2>
	<p>
		Course materials and recordings are for your personal use while you're a
		student and as alumni. Please don't resell or republish them.
	</p>

	<h2>Liability</h2>
	<p>
		We teach engineering skills; we don't guarantee any business outcome. Our
		total liability to you is limited to the fees you've paid us.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
	</p>
</Prose>
